  "helpTitle8": "Your garden & Focus",
  "helpBody8": "Every day you study, your garden grows a little greener.\n\nTrees that grow from studying\n\n• Each new or due word you review waters your tree. Ten waterings grow a study tree in your garden.\n• Choose your study tree in Garden. The more regularly you study, the more species you unlock.\n\nFocus mode\n\n• Set a time, pick a tag (English, Writing, Work…) and start: your tree grows as you focus.\n• Leave the app for more than 30 seconds or give up and the tree withers. Locking the phone keeps it growing.\n• After a session, review a few due words to make it bloom.\n\nComing soon\n\n• Blocking distracting apps while you focus.\n• Relaxing sounds and breathing exercises.\n• A home screen widget with your growing tree and words to review.",
  "helpTitle9": "Listening",
  "helpBody9": "Your ear gets used to English by listening a little every day.\n\nAvailable now\n\n• Listening sources hifive picks for each level, starting with REACH's A1 podcast.\n• Plays right in the app: back or forward 5 seconds, slow it to 0.75× or 0.5×, drag the time bar.\n• The app remembers where you stopped, plays the next episode and ticks the ones you finished.\n• A minute of listening counts that day toward your streak. Suggested goal: 15 minutes a day.\n• Hear a new word? Tap Save word and it shows up in Today's review.\n\nComing soon\n\n• Bilingual subtitles that follow the speech.\n• Shadowing: listen, repeat and record to compare.\n• More sources for every level.",
  "helpTitle10": "Community",
  "helpBody10": "Studying together makes it easier to keep going. Open Decks and tap the globe to enter Community.\n\nShare a deck\n\n• Open a deck, tap ••• then Share deck to get a 6-character code and a link to send.\n• In Decks, tap Enter code, paste the code or link, preview it and add it to your decks.\n• Only the words and meanings are shared, never your progress.\n\nExplore\n\n• Find public decks, popular or newest, and add them to yours.\n• Turn on Public when sharing to list your deck here (the first time, you agree to the community rules).\n• See something wrong? Report the deck or block its creator.\n\nStudy groups\n\n• Make a group, set a goal of study days a week and send friends the invite code.\n• The week shows who studied which day and who met the goal. Reviewing words, a lesson or a minute of listening all count.\n\nClasses\n\n• Teachers make a class, send students the code and set decks with a due date.\n• Students tap Study to add the deck and review as usual; progress updates by itself.\n• Teachers see how many words each student learned, who finished and who is late.",
